            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "No worries about the amount of issues :) Not duplicating module suggestions, feature requests, or bug reports are completely fine.\r\n\r\nI've thought about that while briefly using it. For me the actual tree visualization is rarely useful (if at all).\r\n\r\nMost of the time I wanted to have a more \"linear\" undo history: traverse through the states as they appeared chronologically (i.e. in order they actually appeared). Here is how the idea for the [undo target of 'mini.bracketed'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d6e6a6fb010cc452b491704aa9ecc96a8aa2cde1/doc/mini-bracketed.txt#L446) was born. With this already in place I don't think 'mini.undotree' is on the horizon.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
